<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Crusade</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">captured Jerusalem <a href="/years/1099">1099</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusades">Crusades</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusade</a> was a military expedition by western European Christians that captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> in 1099 and established the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusader states</a>. It took Jerusalem from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a>, and the struggle against the Crusader states later shaped the rise of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-crusade.jpg" alt="First Crusade" width="320" height="308" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peter_the_Hermit.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
